feat(L6): ESLint guard — route mutations through dispatchExecutionTask (#809)

Sovereign Agent Control Level A · L6. Fail-closed lint rules block any
direct PostgREST mutation or RPC call that bypasses the L1 agent
registry, on both the client and the edge-function side.

Plugin: tooling/eslint-plugin-easylocs/
- require-dispatch-execution-task: AST chain walker that detects
  `.from(...).insert|update|delete|upsert(...)` AND the project's
  call-style shorthand `db('table').insert|update|delete|upsert(...)`,
  including `v2db('t')`, `domainDb.x('t')`, `supabase('t')` etc.
  Builder-root identifiers are recognised by name (db|v2db|supabase|sb|
  client|getClient) or `db`/`Db` suffix.
- no-direct-postgrest-mutation: blocks raw fetch POST|PATCH|PUT|DELETE
  to `/rest/v1/...` URLs.
- no-direct-rpc-mutation: blocks `<builder-root>.rpc('fn', …)` since
  static "read vs write" classification is undecidable. Read-only RPCs
  are exempted via the allow-list with a written reason; mutating RPCs
  must move to dispatchExecutionTask.
- ESM plugin; minimatch consumed via default-export interop.
- All three rules support an `allowlistPath` rule option (per-config
  override), in addition to the EASYLOCS_DISPATCH_ALLOWLIST env var and
  the default repo-root allow-list.

Helpers: the only sanctioned mutation entry points
- src/lib/execution/dispatch.ts — client/SSR side, uses the canonical
  `db.schema('system').rpc('dispatch_execution_task', …)`.
- supabase/functions/_shared/execution/dispatch.ts — Deno/edge side,
  same contract; lazily constructs a service-role client from
  SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
- Both export typed `DispatchedTaskHandle`, `DispatchError`,
  `DispatchExecutionTaskInput`, `DispatchRisk`, `DispatchApprovalPolicy`.

Allow-list: .eslintrc.dispatch-allowlist.json
- 615 pre-L1 exemption entries (snapshot of current sites + global
  exemptions for tests, migrations, orchestrator framework, tooling).
- The `supabase/functions/_shared/execution/**` global exemption
  already covers the new Deno helper.
- Each new exemption requires a written reason + PR review.
- L7 (#814) will progressively shrink this list to zero.

Wiring:
- eslint.config.js loads the local plugin and turns all three rules on
  as errors at repo root for src/** and supabase/functions/**.
- package.json devDeps: file:./tooling/eslint-plugin-easylocs.
- Tests live at src/__tests__/eslint-plugin-easylocs.test.ts so vitest
  picks them up; uses RuleTester with passing + failing fixtures for
  every rule, the bypass cases, AND the `allowlistPath` rule option.

Docs: docs/architecture/dispatch-guard.md describes the contract,
all three rules, allow-list governance, and how to request an
exemption.

